			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Treat unknown method errors as benign for circuit breaker logic\n\nAdvance the Cocoon submodule to treat unrecognized gRPC method names as benign conditions rather than hard circuit breaker failures.\n\nCocoon's GRPCServerService method dispatcher previously counted unknown-method responses as failure events in the circuit breaker counter. When Mountain probes for method names across subsystems that route to Node rather than Cocoon's handler registry — or when the method set evolves independently on each side of the gRPC boundary — these probe responses could trip the circuit breaker open, disrupting legitimate requests.\n\nThe fix filters unknown-method errors from the circuit breaker's failure accounting, allowing only genuine transport or handler errors to trigger breaker state transitions. The unknown-method case still returns a proper error response to the caller, but no longer penalizes the breaker health score.",
			"SHA": "119b4c70e55d325a403ffdbe19fa72efb9076d22"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T20:46:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — storage RPC fix, clean identifiers, tier routing\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, Output, and Wind submodules to fix a storage cache priming regression, restore clean development identifiers, and implement per-subsystem IPC tier routing.\n\nCocoon corrects the RPC method name in the storage cache priming path from `storage:getItems` (kebab-case, object arg) to `Storage.GetItems` (PascalCase, empty array), matching Mountain's RPC dispatcher contract. Without this fix, extensions that read workspace/global state synchronously during `activate()` — Roo Code, Copilot, GitLens — received only defaults after every reload, causing UI state regressions.\n\nMountain restores \"Mountain\" as the crate binary, library, and package name, and the Tauri productName and bundle identifier, replacing the verbose development build descriptors from the prior commit. Gates the Cocoon sidecar launch on both the ExtensionHostCocoon feature flag and the absence of `no_node_host` cfg so the Node vs WebWorker tier is respected at boot. Includes the task type in the task provider Options payload for correct Cocoon task registration, derives Clone on ExtensionCollection for shared terminal env mutation, and adds the zsh shell integration script to the Tauri resource bundle.\n\nOutput introduces per-subsystem tier resolution in the TauriChannel IPC router so channels can route to Mountain (Tauri backend) or Node (Cocoon extension host) independently rather than being governed by the single global `_TierIPC` variable. Routes `tasks` and `auth` to Node by default while keeping most subsystems on Mountain.\n\nWind wires the runtime dispatch layer in TauriMainProcessService that reads per-subsystem tier overrides from env vars and `__LandTiers` globals, routing channels resolved to \"Node\" directly to Cocoon via the `cocoon:request` bridge instead of Mountain. This mirrors the dispatch in Mountain's WindServiceHandlers, completing TIER-SYSTEM Step 4b.\n\nExtension storage now persists correctly across reloads, the development build uses clean identifiers, and the IPC tier routing layer supports per-subsystem routing across the Mountain-Cocoon boundary.",
			"SHA": "cdef6cceabdd3c790f0ac922156e6ad2a967ddbf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:32:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — dev build isolation, module resolution, and dependency fixes\n\nAdvance all six Element submodules to their latest revisions, addressing build artifact, dependency, and module resolution issues across the editor stack.\n\nMountain renames the crate binary, library, package, Tauri productName, and bundle identifier to a verbose development build descriptor (encoding Node 22, VS Code dependency, debug profile, esbuild compiler), preventing binary name and macOS bundle ID collisions with the release build. The Tauri resource bundle expands to include all Sky deployment variant directories that were previously omitted. This enables side-by-side installation and testing of development and release builds.\n\nSky replaces three bare `@codeeditorland/sky` package specifiers in workbench layout entry points (Bundled Electron, standalone Electron, Mountain Tauri) with explicit relative paths resolving to `Function/Sky/Bridge.js`. This ensures deterministic module resolution when the build pipeline does not alias the package name to the Sky source directory, preventing resolution failures or duplicate bridge module copies.\n\nOutput adds the missing `browserslist` dependency to its package manifest, resolving an unhandled peer dependency that could cause build failures in downstream consumers.\n\nCocoon regenerates all compiled JavaScript output to pick up the latest extension-host API fidelity source changes, folding several Target files into a single consolidated bootstrap pipeline routed through `Target/Effect/RPCServer.js`.\n\nMaintain relocates the `IsFreeVarSafe` check and `FindSubstSite` resolution from the main eliminator loop in Inline.rs into `TryBlockPreserve` in mod.rs, where the Preserve-pass text-patching logic actually consumes them. Flattens multi-line function signatures, replaces wildcard destructuring with rest patterns, and reflows doc comments. Behaviour across both Preserve and AST-rebuild paths remains identical.\n\nWind regenerates its TypeScript incremental build metadata file, reflecting updated program structure and declaration maps after module resolution changes in the project.\n\nDevelopment builds now install side-by-side with release builds without bundle identifier conflicts, all workbench entry points resolve the Sky bridge deterministically, and the missing browserslist dependency is restored.",
			"SHA": "ad1d49c23687df1619a1eeb2394db0d376337a91"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:12:27Z",
