				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance submodules — DAP inline, panel persist, tier routing\n\nAdvance all six Element submodules to their latest revisions, bringing inline DAP debugging, webview panel persistence across reloads, and a compile-time tier routing framework to the Mountain-Cocoon gRPC boundary.\n\nCocoon implements `DebugAdapterInlineImplementation` by tracking `debug.didStartSession`/`didTerminateSession` lifecycle events from Mountain and instantiating per-session adapters in-process. Wire `onDidSendMessage` back to Mountain via `debug.dap-response` and dispatch incoming DAP frames from the `ExtHostDebug$sendDAPRequest` gRPC handler. Adapter factories are stashed in `ExtensionRegistry` by debug type for reverse-RPC lookup. Register webview panel serializers via `registerWebviewPanelSerializer` and handle `$serializeAllWebviewPanels`/`$deserializeWebviewPanel` so panels like Live Preview survive `nativeHost:reload`. Update `version` and `isDirty` on `$acceptDocumentChanged` and after document-save notifications in HandleSpecificNotification. Fix BuildGetConfiguration to return the caller's `DefaultValue` when Mountain signals \"no override\" (null).\n\nMountain introduces compile-time tier routing for 16 IPC subsystems (Terminal, SCM, Debug, LanguageFeatures, Search, etc.) via build.rs `EmitTierDefaults`, dispatching commands to Mountain-native handlers or forwarding to Cocoon's gRPC surface through `tier_routes_to_node`. Implement webview panel state persistence across `nativeHost:reload`: serialize all registered panels before the renderer reload and deserialize after Cocoon restarts. Add optional Mist WebSocket transport on port 5051 for high-frequency IPC bypassing the Tauri-invoke + gRPC double hop. Apply a 30-second wall-clock timeout to git subprocess execution so a hung git process releases the effect slot rather than blocking indefinitely. Add crash-safe memento hydration that quarantines corrupted `global.json` to `.corrupted.<ts>` siblings. Fix two discrepancies: align the config change Vine notification payload to send `\"keys\": [key]` (array) instead of `\"key\": key` (string), and update document retrieval from the outdated `GetAllDocuments()` to `GetAll()`.\n\nSky relays `treeView.reveal` from Cocoon extensions by firing a `cel:tree-view:reveal` DOM event and invoking `Views.openView(viewId)` on the workbench service layer.\n\nOutput unconditionally applies MacTitlebarOffset and PartZIndex CSS injections regardless of the `DisableUIFixes` flag, and clears stale Configuration artifacts.\n\nRest normalises shell redirection spacing (`2>/dev/null`) and case branch indentation across Bench.sh, prepublishOnly.sh, and run_tests.sh.\n\nWind removes stale generated TypeScript artifacts (ServiceCatalog, bridge shapes, ~500 IAsteriskUpstream interface definitions) superseded by regenerated daily builds.\n\nDebug adapters that register programmatically, extension webview panels, and configuration-change reactivity now work reliably across the Mountain <-> Cocoon gRPC boundary.",
			"SHA": "bfd45298a48c7131233e59a856fb310ec0bf9137"
		}
	],
